# ImotSync API: example requests, for Visual Studio 2022 (.http files) and VS Code's REST
# Client extension. One request, "Upload two photos", works in REST Client only: Visual
# Studio cannot put a file into a multipart body. Its comment shows how to upload with
# curl.exe or Swagger UI instead; every other request works in both editors.
#
# Run them top to bottom: "login" stores the token that every later request sends,
# "createProperty" the id of the new property, and "photos" the ids of its photos, which
# the reorder and delete requests use.
# The demo accounts come from the seed (npm run db:seed); the photo paths point to seeded
# placeholder photos, change them to any JPEG, PNG, WebP or AVIF files you like.
# Full reference: {{host}}/api/docs (Swagger UI).

@host = http://localhost:3000
@api = {{host}}/api

### Health check (public)
GET {{api}}/health

### Log in as the demo admin (public; about 10 attempts per 15 minutes per IP)
# @name login
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@imotsync.local",
  "password": "demo1234"
}

### Current user
GET {{api}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### List properties: active or draft apartments in Sofia, most expensive first
GET {{api}}/properties?status=active,draft&type=apartment&city=Sofia&sort=-price&page=1&pageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Search (reference code, title, city, district) and portal state: "лозенец", URL-encoded
GET {{api}}/properties?q=%D0%BB%D0%BE%D0%B7%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%B5%D1%86&portal=bazar&portalStatus=published
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Property detail, with photos and portal listings
GET {{api}}/properties/1
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Create a property (refCode is optional: without it the server assigns IS-<id>)
# @name createProperty
POST {{api}}/properties
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "apartment",
  "dealType": "sale",
  "city": "Sofia",
  "district": "Lozenets",
  "title": "Двустаен апартамент с южно изложение",
  "price": 189000,
  "areaM2": 72.5,
  "rooms": 2,
  "floor": 3,
  "totalFloors": 6,
  "description": "Example property created from requests.http."
}

### Update it: change the price, clear the title (null clears a field)
PATCH {{api}}/properties/{{createProperty.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "price": 184500,
  "title": null,
  "status": "active"
}

### Upload two photos (VS Code REST Client only; multipart field "photos", 1-20 files, 15 MB each)
# In Visual Studio 2022, upload with Swagger UI ({{host}}/api/docs, "Try it out") or with
# curl.exe from the api folder, filling in the accessToken from "login" and the id from
# "createProperty":
#   curl.exe -H "Authorization: Bearer <accessToken>" -F "photos=@uploads/demo/is-00001-1.jpg" -F "photos=@uploads/demo/is-00001-2.jpg" http://localhost:3000/api/properties/<id>/images
POST {{api}}/properties/{{createProperty.response.body.$.id}}/images
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=ImotSyncBoundary

--ImotSyncBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="photos"; filename="living-room.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./uploads/demo/is-00001-1.jpg
--ImotSyncBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="photos"; filename="kitchen.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./uploads/demo/is-00001-2.jpg
--ImotSyncBoundary--

### The new property with its photos (after the upload; the next two requests use its photo ids)
# @name photos
GET {{api}}/properties/{{createProperty.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Reorder the photos: swap the two uploaded above (the list must name every photo once)
PUT {{api}}/properties/{{createProperty.response.body.$.id}}/images/order
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "imageIds": [
    {{photos.response.body.$.images[1].id}},
    {{photos.response.body.$.images[0].id}}
  ]
}

### Delete one photo
DELETE {{api}}/properties/{{createProperty.response.body.$.id}}/images/{{photos.response.body.$.images[0].id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Delete the property (409 while it is published or pending on a portal)
DELETE {{api}}/properties/{{createProperty.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### OpenAPI document (public)
GET {{api}}/openapi.json
